{"body": "This adds a new method to the public API, Table.metadataAsTable that returns the table's manifest entries as a table. This provides access to file-level metadata in query engines that can read manifest files as data files.\nThis also exposes metadata tables through BaseMetastoreTableOperations under a special table name ending with $entries.", "date": "2019-02-15T21:30:35Z", "hash": "sha256:a92f4c46c1328a970c24", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#103", "meta": {"additions": 459, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-07-03T21:29:35Z", "comments": 4, "deletions": 71, "draft": false, "files": ["api/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/Table.java", "api/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/expressions/ResidualEvaluator.java", "api/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/transforms/TestResiduals.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseMetastoreTables.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseTable.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseTableScan.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseTransaction.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/DataFiles.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/DataTableScan.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/MetadataTable.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/MetadataTableScan.java"], "n_files": 11, "number": 103, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2019-02-26T05:04:09Z", "by": "rdsr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T17:14:07Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-04-23T05:05:53Z", "by": "xabriel", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "closed", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2019-07-03T21:29:35Z"}, "people": ["rdblue"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Add Table.metadataAsTable", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/103"}
{"body": "This PR contains benchmarks for the Spark data source in Iceberg. The main goal is to compare its performance to the built-in file source in Spark.\nScenarios\n\nReading flat and nested Parquet data without any filters/projections\nReading flat and nested Parquet data with a projection\nReading flat and nested Parquet data with a filter\nWriting flat and nested Parquet data\n\nHow to Execute\nEach benchmark describes how it can be executed in its Javadoc.\nA sample command is illustrated below (ensure the output directory exists):\n./gradlew :iceberg-spark:jmh -PjmhIncludeRegex=SparkParquetFlatDataReadBenchmark -PjmhOutputPath=benchmark/parquet-flat-data-read-benchmark-result.txt\n\nSummary\n\nIceberg DS is V2 and the file source is still V1, which complicates the comparison.\nAdding support for vectorized execution in Iceberg is important. Right now, the file source supports vectorized execution on flat data only.\nThe Parquet reader in Iceberg handles nested data more efficiently.\nIceberg can boost the performance of highly selective queries by leveraging file stats.\nSpark implements nested schema pruning only for the file source, which is odd and should be fixed.\nSpark does not push down filters on nested columns to data sources. There is an ongoing effort to add this functionality in Spark 3.0.\n\nOverall, it seems Iceberg Parquet reader and writer are more efficient but it is important to add vectorized execution. Also, it will make sense to redo the benchmarks once the file source is migrated to DS V2.\nOpen Questions\nWays to run\nThe recommended way to run JMH benchmarks is via Maven or Gradle. However, we can still try integrating into JUnit if it gives us more flexibility.\nMaterializing Datasets\nOne way to materialize Datasets in Java:\nds.foreach(record -> {});\n\nThis approach computes the underlying rdd as follows:\nlazy val rdd: RDD[T] = {\n  val objectType = exprEnc.deserializer.dataType\n  rddQueryExecution.toRdd.mapPartitions { rows =>\n    rows.map(_.get(0, objectType).asInstanceOf[T])\n  }\n}\n\nThe current way looks a bit ugly:\nds.queryExecution().toRdd().toJavaRDD().foreach(record -> {});\n\nHowever, it should be more efficient. It computes the underlying rdd as follows:\n/** Internal version of the RDD. Avoids copies and has no schema */\nlazy val toRdd: RDD[InternalRow] = executedPlan.execute()\n\nDocumentation\nWe need proper documentation on how to run/extend/create benchmarks.", "date": "2019-02-18T18:59:46Z", "hash": "sha256:96f4469a7d27581480d9", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#105", "meta": {"additions": 1805, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-06-12T22:18:53Z", "comments": 13, "deletions": 1, "draft": false, "files": ["build.gradle", "gradle.properties", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkBenchmarkUtil.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/data/parquet/SparkParquetReadersFlatDataBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/data/parquet/SparkParquetReadersNestedDataBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/data/parquet/SparkParquetWritersFlatDataBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/data/parquet/SparkParquetWritersNestedDataBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/Action.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/IcebergSourceBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/IcebergSourceFlatDataBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/IcebergSourceNestedDataBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/parquet/IcebergSourceFlatParquetDataFilterBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/parquet/IcebergSourceFlatParquetDataReadBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/parquet/IcebergSourceFlatParquetDataWriteBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/parquet/IcebergSourceNestedParquetDataFilterBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/parquet/IcebergSourceNestedParquetDataReadBenchmark.java", "spark/src/jmh/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/source/parquet/IcebergSourceNestedParquetDataWriteBenchmark.java"], "merged_at": "2019-06-12T22:18:53Z", "merged_by": "danielcweeks", "n_files": 17, "number": 105, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 5, "updated_at": "2019-06-12T22:18:53Z"}, "people": ["aokolnychyi"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Basic Benchmarks for Iceberg Spark Data Source", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/105"}
{"body": "GenericDataFile.copy should copy maps and lists. Because containers are reused while reading, not copying inner lists and maps causes instances in scan tasks to have incorrect data and can cause concurrent modification exceptions.\nSplit planning correctness was not affected by this bug because it happens before the data file instance is copied and reused.", "date": "2019-02-18T22:56:12Z", "hash": "sha256:c16e33c8578df7cc9341", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#106", "meta": {"additions": 20, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-03-06T00:21:17Z", "comments": 5, "deletions": 6, "draft": false, "files": ["core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/GenericDataFile.java"], "merged_at": "2019-03-06T00:21:17Z", "merged_by": "rdblue", "n_files": 1, "number": 106, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2019-02-19T08:03:32Z", "by": "fbocse", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-20T21:45:38Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-22T22:44:21Z", "by": "fbocse", "state": "APPROVED"}], "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2019-03-06T00:21:17Z"}, "people": ["rdblue"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Deep copy maps and lists in GenericDataFile.", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/106"}
