{"body": "This PR fixes issue reported at #99\nWith this change filtering on complex predicates returns rows:\nscala> spark.sql(\"select * from people_iceberg_complex where friends['Josh'] == 10\").show()\n19/02/22 14:42:30 WARN scheduler.TaskSetManager: Stage 16 contains a task of very large size (113 KB). The maximum recommended task size is 100 KB.\n+---+----+--------------------+\n|age|name|             friends|\n+---+----+--------------------+\n| 30|Andy|[Josh -> 10, Bisw...|\n+---+----+--------------------+\n\nscala> spark.sql(\"select * from people_iceberg_complex where friends['Josh'] == 10\").explain()\n== Physical Plan ==\n*(1) Project [age#25, name#26, friends#27]\n+- *(1) Filter ((friends#27[Josh] = 10) && isnotnull(friends#27))\n   +- *(1) ScanV2 iceberg[age#25, name#26, friends#27] (Filters: [isnotnull(friends#27)], Options: [path=iceberg-people-complex,paths=[]])", "date": "2019-02-22T14:43:56Z", "hash": "sha256:a5811e25860f899cc8d4", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#110", "meta": {"additions": 39, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-02-24T19:03:36Z", "comments": 5, "deletions": 1, "draft": false, "files": ["parquet/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/parquet/ParquetMetricsRowGroupFilter.java", "parquet/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/parquet/TestMetricsRowGroupFilter.java"], "merged_at": "2019-02-24T19:03:36Z", "merged_by": "rdblue", "n_files": 2, "number": 110, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2019-02-22T17:17:49Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-22T17:27:19Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-22T17:27:52Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-23T15:59:41Z", "by": "prodeezy", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "merged", "thumbs_up": 1, "updated_at": "2019-02-24T19:04:02Z"}, "people": ["prodeezy"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "Fix Iceberg Parquet Reader scanning when filtering on nested types", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/110"}
{"body": "This addresses #36 by splitting files at target split size before bin packing.  This does break the tests under com.netflix.iceberg.spark.source.TestFilteredScan which assume a split per partition,. I'm currently unclear how these tests should be handled. Should we keep the assumption around the number of tasks created or should we replace them with something else? If we can decide on how we'll handle the assumption around number of tasks, I can add tests to test out this feature.", "date": "2019-02-25T03:48:28Z", "hash": "sha256:7d969fe0df64aa174756", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#111", "meta": {"additions": 438, "base": "master", "closed_at": "2019-03-04T03:04:36Z", "comments": 13, "deletions": 8, "draft": false, "files": ["api/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/FileFormat.java", "api/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/FileScanTask.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseFileScanTask.java", "core/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/BaseTableScan.java", "core/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/avro/TestAvroSplitScan.java", "core/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/hadoop/TestHadoopCommits.java", "parquet/src/main/java/com/netflix/iceberg/parquet/ParquetMetricsRowGroupFilter.java", "parquet/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/parquet/TestMetricsRowGroupFilter.java", "parquet/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/parquet/TestParquetSplitScan.java", "spark/src/test/java/com/netflix/iceberg/spark/source/TestFilteredScan.java"], "n_files": 10, "number": 111, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2019-02-25T19:28:44Z", "by": "aokolnychyi", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T03:42:17Z", "by": "rdsr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T17:16:16Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T17:19:07Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T17:20:26Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T17:22:22Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2019-02-26T17:22:58Z", "by": "rdblue", "state": "